.SH COMPLETE SUBCOMMAND
.nf
\fBfish\-lsp\fR \fBcomplete\fR [\fB\-\-names\fR] [\fB\-\-toggles\fR] [\fB\-\-fish\fR] [\fB\-\-features\fR]
                  [\fB\-\-env\-variables\fR] [\fB\-\-env\-variable\-names\fR]
                  [\fB\-\-names\-with\-summary\fR] [\fB\-\-abbreviations\fR]
.fi
.P
Provide completions for the \fBfish\-lsp\fP
.P
.TP
\fB\-\-names\fP
.br
show the feature names of the completions
.TP
\fB\-\-toggles\fP
.br
show the feature names of the completions
.TP
\fB\-\-fish\fP
.br
show fish script
.TP
\fB\-\-features\fP
.br
show features
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-variables\fP
.br
show env variable completions
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-variable\-names\fP
.br
show env variable names
.TP
\fB\-\-names\-with\-summary\fP
.br
show the names with the summary for the completions
.TP
\fB\-\-abbreviations\fP
.br
show the 'fish\-lsp' subcommand abbreviations
.P
.SS Examples

